WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:08.326
A live race now marks the riders who leave or drop out: DNF, in last place, on every

00:00:08.326 --> 00:00:09.036
board.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.295
MarcoVelo was eighth. The next second the board shows them last, faint, with DNF

00:00:15.295 --> 00:00:16.713
where the gap was.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:27.591
Pressing Leave tells the session at once, and every rider gets the new standings

00:00:27.591 --> 00:00:29.254
without waiting a second.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.960
A rider silent for fifteen seconds is marked DNF; one gone thirty seconds is removed

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.509
and cannot rejoin.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.674
The board joins at tablet width; on a phone, the race keeps your place beside the

00:00:53.674 --> 00:00:54.317
power.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:07.609
What the tests prove: leavers DNF at once, silence and lost connections caught, and

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:09.002
DNF always last.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.869
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:17.214 --> 00:01:21.726
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:21.726 --> 00:01:23.397
every hill and interval.

00:01:23.742 --> 00:01:28.920
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.368
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:37.358
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:40.196
A custom workout lives under Profile.
